From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MichaIng <micha@dietpi.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: t527-orangepi-4a: add PHY ID compatible

The YT8531 PHY is powered via phy-supply (cldo4), which the MAC driver
enables right before the MDIO bus is registered, and its reset line is
only handled once the PHY device exists. With the generic C22 compatible,
the PHY ID is read from a PHY which is still powering up or in reset. The
read randomly returns 0xffff (no PHY device, "cannot attach to PHY (error:
-ENODEV)"), 0x0 (Generic PHY bound instead of YT8531) or the correct ID.

Add the explicit PHY ID compatible, so the PHY device is created without
reading the ID, and the reset sequence runs before the PHY driver probes.

Signed-off-by: MichaIng <micha@dietpi.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -121,7 +121,8 @@ &gpu {
 
 &mdio1 {
 	ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@1 {
-		compatible = "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
+		compatible = "ethernet-phy-id4f51.e91b",
+			     "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
 		reg = <1>;
 		interrupts-extended = <&pio 8 16 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>; /* PI16 */
 		reset-gpios = <&pio 8 15 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PI15 */
-- 
